  "finalCues": [
    {
      "verse": 1,
      "text": "A good name is more desirable than great riches; to be esteemed is better than silver or gold.",
      "start": 1.36,
      "end": 8.712
    },
    {
      "verse": 2,
      "text": "Rich and poor have this in common: The LORD is the Maker of them all.",
      "start": 9.4,
      "end": 14.312
    },
    {
      "verse": 3,
      "text": "The prudent see danger and take refuge, but the simple keep going and pay the penalty.",
      "start": 15.2,
      "end": 20.744
    },
    {
      "verse": 4,
      "text": "Humility is the fear of the LORD; its wages are riches and honor and life.",
      "start": 21.4,
      "end": 27.496
    },
    {
      "verse": 5,
      "text": "In the paths of the wicked are snares and pitfalls, but those who would preserve their life stay far from them.",
      "start": 28.312,
      "end": 34.856
    },
    {
      "verse": 6,
      "text": "Start children off on the way they should go, and even when they are old they will not turn from it.",
      "start": 35.82,
      "end": 41.928
    },
    {
      "verse": 7,
      "text": "The rich rule over the poor, and the borrower is slave to the lender.",
      "start": 42.82,
      "end": 47.624
    },
    {
      "verse": 8,
      "text": "Whoever sows injustice reaps calamity, and the rod they wield in fury will be broken.",
      "start": 48.3,
      "end": 54.6
    },
    {
      "verse": 9,
      "text": "The generous will themselves be blessed, for they share their food with the poor.",
      "start": 55.36,
      "end": 59.976
    },
    {
      "verse": 10,
      "text": "Drive out the mocker, and out goes strife; quarrels and insults are ended.",
      "start": 60.58,
      "end": 66.088
    },
    {
      "verse": 11,
      "text": "One who loves a pure heart and who speaks with grace will have the king for a friend.",
      "start": 67.06,
      "end": 72.584
    },
    {
      "verse": 12,
      "text": "The eyes of the LORD keep watch over knowledge, but he frustrates the words of the unfaithful.",
      "start": 73.32,
      "end": 79.336
    },
    {
      "verse": 13,
      "text": "The sluggard says, “There’s a lion outside! I’ll be killed in the public square!”",
      "start": 80.483,
      "end": 85.864
    },
    {
      "verse": 14,
      "text": "The mouth of an adulterous woman is a deep pit; a man who is under the LORD’s wrath falls into it.",
      "start": 86.12,
      "end": 92.488
    },
    {
      "verse": 15,
      "text": "Folly is bound up in the heart of a child, but the rod of discipline will drive it far away.",
      "start": 93.44,
      "end": 99.272
    },
    {
      "verse": 16,
      "text": "One who oppresses the poor to increase his wealth and one who gives gifts to the rich—both come to poverty.",
      "start": 99.7,
      "end": 107.4
    },
    {
      "verse": 17,
      "text": "Pay attention and turn your ear to the sayings of the wise; apply your heart to what I teach,",
      "start": 110.461,
      "end": 116.24
    },
    {
      "verse": 18,
      "text": "for it is pleasing when you keep them in your heart and have all of them ready on your lips.",
      "start": 116.62,
      "end": 121.832
    },
    {
      "verse": 19,
      "text": "So that your trust may be in the LORD, I teach you today, even you.",
      "start": 122.06,
      "end": 127.048
    },
    {
      "verse": 20,
      "text": "Have I not written thirty sayings for you, sayings of counsel and knowledge,",
      "start": 127.2,
      "end": 132.0
    },
    {
      "verse": 21,
      "text": "teaching you to be honest and to speak the truth, so that you bring back truthful reports to those you serve?",
      "start": 132.281,
      "end": 138.952
    },
    {
      "verse": 22,
      "text": "Do not exploit the poor because they are poor and do not crush the needy in court,",
      "start": 141.661,
      "end": 146.68
    },
    {
      "verse": 23,
      "text": "for the LORD will take up their case and will exact life for life.",
      "start": 146.8,
      "end": 150.984
    },
    {
      "verse": 24,
      "text": "Do not make friends with a hot-tempered person, do not associate with one easily angered,",
      "start": 153.42,
      "end": 159.58
    },
    {
      "verse": 25,
      "text": "or you may learn their ways and get yourself ensnared.",
      "start": 159.58,
      "end": 162.984
    },
    {
      "verse": 26,
      "text": "Do not be one who shakes hands in pledge or puts up security for debts;",
      "start": 165.102,
      "end": 169.519
    },
    {
      "verse": 27,
      "text": "if you lack the means to pay, your very bed will be snatched from under you.",
      "start": 169.84,
      "end": 174.6
    },
    {
      "verse": 28,
      "text": "Do not move an ancient boundary stone set up by your ancestors.",
      "start": 177.32,
      "end": 181.48
    },
    {
      "verse": 29,
      "text": "Do you see someone skilled in their work? They will serve before kings; they will not serve before officials of low rank.",
      "start": 184.36,
      "end": 192.85
    }
  ],
